	(text_box "K1401 patient relay (made to order, DPDT >= 5 kV, cold-switched) and J1401 pad connector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 152.84 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "29a8bcee-1e64-585e-821f-5a6f0626a93c")
	)
	(text_box "At rest (coil off): PT_PAD_A -> NC_A -> PT_FE_A and PT_PAD_B -> NC_B -> PT_FE_B: the pads see only the two front ends (15, 16).\nEnergised: pads -> NO -> HV_OUT_A/B (bridge, 13). The relay is closed and opened with no current (the sequencer on 12 orders it); it\nmust CARRY 65 A peak for <= 15.5 ms, >= 100 A for 20 ms, 465 A for <= 5 us in a fault [UNVERIFIED for every candidate: no maker\npublishes a pulse/carry rating].\nCandidate search (notes §4): G17 (the design's reference) is a 7.5 kV SF6 relay with 1.0 ohm max contact resistance, 10 A carry, 12\nohm/12 W 100 ms coil and is no longer in Sensata's catalogue. Best real basis: Sensata/Gigavac G12-12Vdc (DPDT vacuum, 8 kV operating\n/ 10 kV test, 20 mOhm, 10 A carry, 15/9 ms, 12 V 60 ohm coil, -55..+125 C). NO catalogue HV relay has an auxiliary contact: the aux\ncontact is a made-to-order requirement (§B7.2), linked to BOTH poles so a single welded pole is seen (fault 29).\nTerminal numbers 1-10 are project numbers (none published). Coil supply below is sized for the worst coil considered (12 ohm, 12 W,\nG17 class); with a 60 ohm G12-class coil it simply runs at 100 % duty (2.4 W).\nJ1401 (made to order): PAD_A/PAD_B energy contacts (HV_PULSE class, PT_PAD_*), three separated LV contacts: ID (1-Wire DS2431-class\nEEPROM in the pad plug, D-57), ID_RET (= GND), PRESENT (looped to ID_RET inside the plug). No test points on PT_* (R9)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 152.84 27.908)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "97a9c92f-2265-5dbc-a5c9-cd9631886446")
	)
	(text_box "Pad ID (1-Wire) and presence lines: series R + TVS at the connector; aux contact -> K_REST_N"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.56 25.4 0)
		(size 175.85 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d0949415-1194-56c1-abb3-8c0929e61aba")
	)
	(text_box "PAD_ID_1W: TVS TPD1E10B06 (bidirectional, VRWM 5.5 V, 12 pF, 6 A 8/20 us) at the contact, then 100 ohm series to the net (2.2 k pull-up on 04). 100 ohm x 4\nmA slave sink = 0.4 V: inside a 3.3 V master's VIL. ADI's own series-R recommendation (DS9503 class) could not be read [UNVERIFIED].\nPAD_PRESENT_N: loop to GND in the plug; TVS at the contact, 1 k series (pull-up 100 k on 04: low = 33 mV). Unplugged / open / unsoldered = high = 'not\nfitted' (safe reading).\nK_REST_N: aux contact AUX_NC closes K_AUX to GND only at rest. 1 k series + TVS so a fault inside the HV relay body cannot put more than a clamp-limited\ncurrent onto the LV board. Open contact, unfitted relay or broken wire = high = 'NOT at rest' (main faults, F-6). See notes 'Contract issues' about what an\nopen contact means to the sequencer (R11)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.56 31.75 0)
		(size 175.85 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f3ce5dcb-6de5-59bd-b975-1adbb554d312")
	)
	(text_box "Coil supply input disconnect: Q1401 P-FET, slow turn-on, driven by K_EN (zero standby draw)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 394.73 25.4 0)
		(size 255.745 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8d83f874-d527-56c2-8bb5-f4b5f1cb8eed")
	)
	(text_box "A boost converter passes VIN to VOUT when disabled (TPS61089 datasheet §8.3.2), so without this switch the reservoir and DRV110 would sit at VBAT_SYS in standby (aluminium-cap leakage up to 0.5 mA rated, DRV110 0.25 mA) —\nagainst the zero-standby budget of design §11. Q1401 DMP3013SFV (-30 V, VGS +/-25 V, 17 mOhm max at -4.5 V).\nK_EN high -> Q1402 (2N7002, 3.3 V gate) pulls K_PG down through R1402 47 k. Miller capacitor C1401 68 nF sets the drain slew: ~ (7.4-2.5) V / 47 k ~ 0.1 mA minus 25 uA through R1401 -> ~1.1 V/ms -> reservoir precharge current\n6.6 mF x 1.1 V/ms ~ 7 A for ~ 6-7 ms [EST; Q1401 SOA at ~3.7 V x 7 A x 7 ms UNVERIFIED].\nK_EN low -> R1401 100 k pulls the gate to the source; Q1401 off in a few ms. R1404 100 k is the contract's K_EN default (coil off)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 394.73 31.75 0)
		(size 255.745 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3a889531-a0cb-5a60-a5f9-a57d1032139c")
	)
	(text_box "12 V boost U1401 TPS61089 (VIN 2.7-12 V, VOUT 4.5-12.6 V, 7 A switch), EN = K_EN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 105.378 0)
		(size 253.29 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "909ab22a-dcf7-53f9-bab5-74849f91db6d")
	)
	(text_box "FB: VREF 1.212 V; R1407 887 k / R1408 100 k -> 11.96 V (OVP 12.7-13.6 V). FSW: R1405 301 k FSW-to-SW -> ~500 kHz (datasheet point). ILIM: R1406 127 k -> 8.1 A typ (7.3-8.9 A): fast reservoir charge.\nLoad: coil peak 0.86 A x 11.6 V ~ 10 W + DRV110/sense ~0.3 W -> ~2.1 A in at 5.5 V, 1.6 A at 7.4 V [CALC]; plus reservoir charging at the current limit for ~10 ms after K_EN (input up to ~8 A, inside the pack protector's 30\nA, OUTSIDE the design's 2.0 A budget: notes).\nL1401 2.2 uH (datasheet nominal; Coilcraft XAL7030-222, Isat >= 9 A [BK, verify]). COUT 3 x 22 uF ceramic on K_VBOOST (datasheet 10-1000 uF effective); the 6.6 mF reservoir sits behind D1401 so the boost loop sees it only\nwhile charging it [loop behaviour while charging UNVERIFIED: SIM].\nEN: K_EN through R1413 100 k (R7: reader may be unpowered while its input ramps); internal 800 k pull-down -> 2.9 V high, 1.2 V threshold."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 111.728 0)
		(size 253.29 14.954)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8fc1dafc-f2c4-570b-947f-d5152327905a")
	)
	(text_box "Hold-up reservoir K_VCOIL: D1401 + 2 x 3300 uF 16 V (6.6 mF) — relay stays closed >= 30 ms if the boost or VBAT_SYS fails"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.01 118.235 0)
		(size 208.28 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
