				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8489d6dc-d857-51a3-a850-f3c91a7c9935")
	)
	(text_box "Sized [CALC, notes §3.5] for the worst case: boost lost at the earliest sequence start (~20 ms after K_EN) while the DRV110 is still in its 33 ms peak phase (coil resistive, tau =\nR_coil x C), then hold at 0.5 A regulated. Hot coil 15 ohm (hold needs >= 7.8 V): ~48 ms; boost lost during hold: ~60 ms; both > 30 ms. 4.4 mF would leave ~30 ms with no margin; the\ndesign's 1.7 mF assumed a constant 3 W draw and no peak phase.\nPrecharge happens through Q1401 slew (see input group); standby voltage 0 V. Discharge after a shock through the DRV110 supply (~0.25 mA) and leakage.\nNichicon UHE1C332MHD: 16 V, 3300 uF, 12.5 x 35.5 mm, -40..+105 C; 13.6 V worst-case OVP = 85 % of rating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.01 124.585 0)
		(size 208.28 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "29725a0c-7359-5c9d-b695-a55882aef268")
	)
	(text_box "Coil economiser U1402 DRV110A (peak 0.86 A for 33 ms, hold 0.5 A, 20 kHz) + Q1403 + fast-release clamp"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 527.61 118.235 0)
		(size 253.635 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f83af42e-3a20-56de-93ac-bbec29905d4b")
	)
	(text_box "RSENSE R1419 0.25 ohm. IPEAK = 0.9 V x 66.67 k / RPEAK / RSENSE: R1415 280 k -> 0.857 A (>= G17 pick-up 8 V / 12 ohm = 0.67 A). IHOLD = 0.15 V x 66.67 k / RHOLD / RSENSE: R1416 80.6 k -> 0.496 A (> G17 worst drop-out 5 V /\n12 ohm = 0.42 A; 'hold at ~50 %', design §B7.2). Hold sense voltage 124 mV (> 30 mV minimum). KEEP C1414 0.33 uF -> 33 ms peak (tKEEP = C x 1e5 s/F): covers pull-in while K_VCOIL is still rising from the battery level. OSC\nto GND -> 20 kHz default (datasheet Eq. 4 text).\nVIN: R1414 1 k from K_VCOIL + C1413 4.7 uF (datasheet Table 3: 1 k at 12 V with EN toggled; internal clamp 15 V; VIN >= 6 V). OUT drives Q1403 gate at VIN (<= 13 V): Q1403 DMN3027LFG has VGS +/-25 V (a +/-12 V part would be\noverstressed). R1420 100 k holds the gate low when U1402 is unpowered.\nEN: K_EN via R1417 10 k with R1418 47 k to GND (the DRV110 EN pin floats HIGH internally: this keeps it low when K_EN is low or open). K_EN low -> gate off at once.\nFast release: coil current at turn-off goes K_COIL_L -> D1402 SS34 -> D1403 SMBJ10A (VBR 11.1-12.3 V) -> K_VCOIL: ~ -12.8 V across the coil instead of -0.5 V (release time is in the timing budget, R-12). The same path\nfreewheels the 20 kHz hold PWM (fast decay: more ripple and loss in hold, acceptable for <= 90 ms). Drain peak = 13.2 V + 12.3 V + ~1 V + 0.5 V ~ 27 V < 30 V VDS (90 %) [CALC].\nThe 90 ms on-time cap and the <= 60 ms start window are on 12_bridge_logic (contract §8); this sheet only obeys K_EN. STATUS (open drain) is not read: no contract net."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 527.61 124.585 0)
		(size 253.635 21.431)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
